  "mathematics": {
    "UB": [
      "Coset G1/G2/G3 is an exact equivalence in the finite-rank setting, including every partial flag and its residue; flag transitivity is derived from the stated primitive residue actions.",
      "The residual maximality induction proves complement-indexed generation and full subset intersections without finite-group assumptions.",
      "The weighted forest is finite with positive finite block sizes. Unique tree paths give intersections, laminar rooted cuts give simultaneous flag representatives, and the overgroup lemma handles equal halves and singleton exceptions."
    ],
    "B1": [
      "All four Theorem 1 clauses are recovered through the retained B97 classification and uniqueness, the explicit tree model, and reconstruction from its line graph.",
      "Even-rank PRI, the exact balanced-cut/middle condition, QPRI and RPRI/star criteria keep their distinct meanings."
    ],
    "B2": [
      "W1 is the independent-family upper bound and extremal-generation implication; W2 is a separately retained omission-subgroup trichotomy with CFSG dependence. A false blanket converse in the source is not imported.",
      "The block-kernel argument excludes the imprimitive block-size-two alternative at n >= 7. Parity-twisted markings have the explicitly proved subgroup formula and intersection property.",
      "The three counts distinguish literal ordinary markings, literal twisted markings, and individual 3-cycle inversion classes. Their combinatorial encodings are supplied.",
      "The maximal-rank geometry converse assumes the declared firm, residually connected, flag-transitive source geometry. It proves weak residual primitivity by the panel intersections and residual generation; it does not add that property as a hypothesis."
    ],
    "B3": [
      "The subgroup correspondence is an actual incidence-preserving typed coset quotient, with intersection and maximality intervals preserved.",
      "Zorn supplies maximal overgroups under relative finite generation. The unrestricted infinite nongeneration converse has the stated Prüfer-group counterexample.",
      "The geometric infinite-group theorem obtains relative finite generation from its finite maximal-subgroup ladder before using the nongeneration argument.",
      "Finite p-group geometries are coordinate hyperplane quotients with Borel equal to the kernel; the count is for indexed hyperplane families rather than automorphism orbits.",
      "The residue Frattini test is only necessary. The action kernel is core_G(B), equal to the intersection of the parabolic cores. C10/C11 are mapped correctly by the additive delta."
    ],
    "B4": [
      "The weighted-star construction gives all chambers, residues and the exact panel size. The k = 1, n = 3 thin boundary is preserved.",
      "The bipartite Kneser distance, diameter and gonality formulas are proved by replacement bounds and realizing walks.",
      "Johnson graph reconstruction and neighborhood synchronization prove the typed group. The Kneser filtration and least-eigenspace equality prove that all uncolored graph automorphisms permute the type classes.",
      "The corrected S7 x S3 group belongs to the explicit 63-vertex example. This does not refute an existential assertion about a different locally Desargues graph."
    ]
  },
